## 3. AI-generated disclosure standard (§4) — measured on the delivered pixels

**Method.** The badge is composited as a fixed layer (not requested from the
model), then every delivered file is re-opened and the badge region re-measured.
Reels are additionally verified by **decoding frames back out of the encoded
MP4**, so the check is on the shippable artifact, not the pre-encode frame.

| Asset class | Count | Contrast (AA needs 4.5) | Lower-right | Unclipped | Phone-preview |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| Carousel slides (Tue) | 5 | 5.33 : 1 | 5/5 | 5/5 | 6.52–7.41 : 1 PASS |
| Static (Fri) | 1 | 5.33 : 1 | 1/1 | 1/1 | 7.31 : 1 PASS |
| Reel masters (decoded frames) | 5 | **5.07–5.08 : 1 min** | 5/5 | 5/5 | see below |
| Reel shot frames | 20 | 5.08 : 1 | all | all | see below |
| Reel covers (rebuilt) | 5 | 5.04 : 1 | 5/5 | 5/5 | 5.88–6.84 : 1 PASS |

- Badge geometry, reels: `x=733, y=1753, 291×57 px` → right margin **56 px**,
  bottom margin **110 px**, clear of the reel UI zone.
- Badge geometry, 4:5: right margin **56 px**, bottom margin **86 px**.
- §4 phone gate run as an actual downscale + **JPEG q26 round-trip**; all 11
  still deliverables pass with 9–15 % surviving glyph coverage.

### A real defect found and fixed in this run

The first reel encode applied the Ken Burns zoom to frames that **already**
carried the burnt badge. The zoom then moved the badge and cropped it on some
frames: measured contrast collapsed to **2.36 : 1** and it failed §4. That build
was **not** shipped.

Fix: the motion is now applied to the clean generated frame, and the copy +
badge are overlaid as a fixed alpha layer afterwards. Re-measured from decoded
frames: **5.07–5.08 : 1, uniform, unclipped on every frame**. The rejection and
the fix are recorded in `qa_report.json`.

> Carried risk, unchanged from v2: the **supplied anchor sheets themselves carry
> no `AI-generated` disclosure**, which §7.1 requires. If they are ever
> published or reposted they breach §4 today. Recommend the Creative Director
> re-issues them with the label burned in (AAR-7).

