## 5. Global generation blocks (as executed)

**Positive base — appended to every shot prompt.**
> A realistic editorial diary photograph of the same fictional North Indian
> woman, age 22–26, wheatish skin with natural texture, long open dark hair worn
> fully down, a small centred maroon bindi, and silver jhumkas. Warm daylight,
> modest opaque everyday [wardrobe], [activity] in [non-intimate setting],
> neutral eye-level medium framing, natural posture, realistic skin texture,
> respectful lifestyle editorial.

**Exclusion block — appended to every shot prompt (Persona Bible §3, unmodified).**
> Do not change her face, apparent age, complexion, hairline, or facial
> proportions. No tied hair, braid, ponytail, bun, clip-up, or updo. No missing
> maroon bindi or silver jhumkas. No glamorised or sexualised styling; no sheer,
> tight, low-cut, strapless, wet, lingerie-like, or bodycon clothing. No seductive
> pose/expression, reclining, bedroom/bathroom/bed setting, body-focused crop,
> low-angle chest/hip emphasis, or suggestive copy.

**Anchor binding.** Each shot's registered anchor crop (plus its SHA-256) is
supplied as the identity reference on the generation call, so continuity is
provable rather than asserted. The exact per-frame digests are in the QA
evidence bundle.

**Model + method.** `google/gemini-3-pro-image` (image-input, image-output) via
OpenRouter, one call per shot, anchor supplied inline. The disclosure string and
on-image copy are **not** requested from the model; they are composited as a
fixed layer so §4 is deterministic.

